{
  "dom_id": "step-q125422",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "If ${\\int }_{C}z\\,\\text{d}x+x\\,\\text{d}y+y\\,\\text{d}z$ is equivalent to ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ for some piecewise smooth curve $C,$ then $F(x,y,z)=$",
  "worked_solution": "Given a piecewise-smooth path $C$ and a vector field \n\n$$\nF(x,y,z)=P(x,y,z)\\,i+Q(x,y,z)\\,j+R(x,y,z)\\,k\n$$\n\ndefined on $C,$ we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{C}P\\,\\text{d}x+Q\\,\\text{d}y+R\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\nIn our case, $P=z,Q=x,R=y.$ Therefore\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{C}(z\\,i+x\\,j+y\\,k)\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{C}z\\,\\text{d}x+x\\,\\text{d}y+y\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, $F=z\\,i+x\\,j+y\\,k.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
